 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py` (the `brain/` notes don't cover it):\n\n- **`VerbView`** (subclass of `View`) is the class you write with `get()`/`post()`.\n- **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** scans the class for HTTP verb names (`http_method_funcs`) and sets `cls.methods` to the uppercase set, e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`.\n- **`View.to_view_func(name, *args, **kwargs)`** (classmethod) builds the view function:\n  - The inner `view(**kwargs)` instantiates the class, either per request or once if `init_every_request` is `False`, and calls `self.run_view` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n  - It copies `view_class`, `methods`, `provide_automatic_options`, `__name__`, `__doc__` and `__module__` onto the function, and applies any `decorators`.\n- **Registration**: `app.attach_route_rule(\"/counter\", view_func=CounterAPI.to_view_func(\"counter\"))`. The routing layer reads `view.methods` to decide which methods the rule accepts.\n- **`VerbView.run_view(**kwargs)`** does the per-request dispatch. It calls `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and falls back to `get` for `HEAD` when no `head` handler exists. It then calls the handler via `ensure_sync` with the URL variables as kwargs.",
